  partName: Stud (3)
  description: The Stud (3) is a tiny, compact fastener located at the top-center-rear
    of the engine, made of Material.002, serving as a mounting point for various
    engine components, providing a secure and stable connection, and its compact
    shape enables efficient use of space. The Stud (3) is designed to withstand significant
    stress and strain, ensuring the engine's components remain securely attached.
    Interestingly, the Stud (3) is often used in conjunction with other fasteners
    to provide added stability and support.
